'''List of Shikinaisha in Sanuki Province''' (Sanuki no Shikinaisha Ichiran) is a list of {{ill|shrine|shrine|shrine|神社|神社|shrine|shrine|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/shrine|qq=}}s in {{ill|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|讃岐国|讃岐国|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sanuki Province|qq=}} recorded in volumes 9 and 10, “Kamimyōchō, Upper and Lower”, of the {{ill|Engishiki|Engishiki|Engishiki|Engishiki|Engishiki|Engishiki|Engishiki|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki|qq=}} and {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|延喜式神名帳|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|延喜式神名帳|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=}}, including shrines known as {{ill|Shikinaisha|Shikinaisha|Shikinaisha|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|Shikinaisha|Shikinaisha|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|qq=}} and their {{ill|Candidate shrine|Candidate shrine|Candidate shrine|論社|1=candidate shrines|2=ja|3=論社|lt=candidate|論社|Candidate shrine|Candidate shrine|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Candidate shrine|13=User:Immanuelle/candidate shrines|qq=}}, which are classified under {{ill|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|讃岐国|讃岐国|Sanuki Province|Sanuki Province|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sanuki Province|qq=}}.
It also includes shrines known as {{ill|Shikigai‐sha|Shikigai‐sha|Shikigai‐sha|式外社|1=Shikigeisha|式外社|Shikigai‐sha|Shikigai‐sha|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikigai‐sha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikigeisha|qq=}} that existed at the time the ‘Engishiki’ shrine catalogue was compiled but were not recorded in it.
--><!-- The subsequent tables are translated following the same principles with appropriate conversion of internal links and table headings. -->

This is a '''List of Shikinaisha in Sanuki Province'''. Or the list of shrines in [[Sanuki Province]] which is present in the {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|ja|延喜式神名帳|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=}}. On this page we will also cover the {{ill|Shikigeisha|ja|式外社|1=Shikigeisha|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikigeisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikigeisha|qq=}} of [[Sanuki Province]] which are shrines that are known to have existed at that time due to other historical records, such as the [[Rikkokushi]], but for some reason were excluded from the {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|ja|延喜式神名帳|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=}}. We will cover them in a separate list to avoid confusion.
== Shikinaisha (式内社) == In the ‘Engishiki’ shrine catalogue, three groups of major shrines (3 shrines) and 21 groups of minor shrines (21 shrines), a total of 24 shrines, are recorded.
